# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Virtual environments. My venv lives outside the repo, but this catches the
# case where I accidentally create one inside it.
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vim leftovers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vim writes a swap file while a buffer is open and leaves it behind if the
# session is killed - which happens often on Rangpur when an SSH connection
# drops. The extensions run .swp, .swo, .swn and so on as more swaps pile up
# for the same file, so the pattern covers the whole range.
*.swp
*.swo
*.sw[a-z]

# Backup copies vim writes when 'backup' is on, and the undo history files.
*~
*.bak
*.un~
.netrwhist

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Other editors, in case I open the repo locally rather than on the cluster
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS and Linux filesystem clutter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trained model files - THE IMPORTANT ONE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The assignment says not to commit model files, and that committing
# multi-gigabyte files will get the pull request rejected. A GFNet checkpoint
# is tens or hundreds of MB, and git keeps every version forever, so one
# careless 'git add .' during a training run could bloat the repo permanently
# and be awkward to undo.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.onnx
*.pkl
checkpoints/
weights/
runs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Datasets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The assignment says not to commit datasets either. The ADNI data lives at
# /home/groups/comp3710/ADNI and is read from there directly, so it should
# never appear inside the repo - but if I ever symlink or copy it in for a
# local test, these patterns stop it being staged.
data/
dataset/
ADNI/
AD_NC/
*.jpeg
*.jpg
*.nii
*.nii.gz
*.npy
*.npz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SLURM job output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every job writes a .out and .err file. Over a week of runs these add up to
# dozens of near-identical files that say nothing about how the code evolved.
# If a particular log matters for the report I will quote the relevant numbers
# in the README rather than committing the raw file.
logs/
slurm-*.out
slurm-*.err
*.out
*.err

# Files to be ignored for local testing and datasets imported from rangpur to local
# system.
adni_subset/
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT ignored, on purpose
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PNG and SVG files are deliberately absent from the lists above. The README
# needs figures - training curves, prediction overlays, confusion matrices,
# the learned frequency filters - and those have to be committed or the
# documentation marks suffer. The rule I am following: ignore things the code
# produces as a side effect, keep things a reader needs to see.
#
# The *.jpeg and *.jpg patterns above are there to block dataset images. If I
# ever need a .jpg figure in the README, I force it in with:
#     git add -f recognition/GFNet_s4967283/figures/my_figure.jpg
# Better still, save figures as .png so this never comes up.
outputs/
